s to invest up to $50 billion in OpenAI for potential AI partnership and model integration.\\n\\nKey features include home automation (controlling lights, locks, thermostats from various manufacturers), music streaming from multiple services, sports updates across 15 leagues, messaging and calling, food ordering, Amazon Key in-home delivery, severe weather alerts, traffic updates, and Alexa for Business. The Alexa Skills Kit allows third-party developers to create skills, while Alexa Voice Service (AVS) enables manufacturers to integrate Alexa into their own products. In 2019, Alexa began supporting Spanish voice commands, and in 2020, Amazon announced Amitabh Bachchan as a celebrity voice option in India.\", \"key_excerpts\": \"Alexa was largely developed from the British computer scientist William Tunstall-Pedoe's Evi system and a Polish speech synthesizer named Ivona, acquired by Amazon in 2012 and 2013., In 2022, with the division losing several billion dollars per quarter, the company started laying off Alexa employees en masse., In February 2025, Amazon introduced Alexa+, the latest version of their voice assistant, which is powered by generative AI. Alexa+ was announced to be free for all Prime members., In early 2026, Amazon entered advanced discussions to invest up to $50 billion in OpenAI as part of a potential artificial intelligence partnership so that OpenAI's models could be integrated into Amazon's digital assistant Alexa., According to an August 2018 article by The Information, only 2 percent of Alexa owners have used the device to make a purchase during the first seven months of 2018 and of those who made an initial purchase, 90 percent did not make a second purchase.\"}"}}]},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"tool_calls"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":5509,"completion_tokens":735,"total_tokens":6244,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":5504},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":5504,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":5},"system_fingerprint":"fp_9954b31ca7_prod0820_fp8_